# 8-Bit Ripple Carry Adder — XOR/AND/OR CMOS Implementation

## Overview
This implementation of an 8-bit ripple carry adder uses CMOS full-adder circuits designed with XOR, AND, and OR logic. The circuit was designed and simulated using Cadence Virtuoso.

## Design Description
The full-adder circuit generates the Sum and Carry outputs from two input bits and an incoming carry.

The Boolean expressions are:

- **Sum:** A ⊕ B ⊕ Cin
- **Carry-out:** AB + ACin + BCin

Eight full-adder stages are cascaded, with the carry output of each stage connected to the carry input of the next stage.

## Implementation
- Designed CMOS full-adder circuitry using XOR, AND, and OR logic.
- Cascaded eight full-adder stages to construct the 8-bit adder.
- Developed circuit schematics in Cadence Virtuoso.
- Simulated the design to verify sum generation and carry propagation.

